From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 11:22:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] soundwire: qcom: balance runtime PM and hclk in remove

Probe enables runtime PM at its end, but remove never disables it, and
remove releases hclk even when runtime suspend has already released it.

When the controller unbinds and binds again, which on X1E80100 happens
whenever the audio DSP restarts because the whole LPASS chain depends on
clocks the DSP provides, the second probe then runs with runtime PM still
enabled. sdw_bus_master_add() runtime-resumes the controller before its bus
is set up and swrm_runtime_resume() oopses in sdw_bus_exit_clk_stop()
(NULL dereference), so the sound card cannot come back. The unbind itself
warns "mclk already disabled" / "already unprepared".

Disable runtime PM in remove, release hclk only if the controller is still
runtime active, and mark it suspended.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/soundwire/qcom.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
index a3700de68..6c65c7314 100644
--- a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
@@ -1724,9 +1724,22 @@ static int qcom_swrm_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 static void qcom_swrm_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct qcom_swrm_ctrl *ctrl = dev_get_drvdata(&pdev->dev);
+	struct device *dev = &pdev->dev;
 
 	sdw_bus_master_delete(&ctrl->bus);
-	clk_disable_unprepare(ctrl->hclk);
+
+	/*
+	 * Balance the pm_runtime_enable() in probe. Left enabled, the next
+	 * probe after an unbind (the audio DSP restarting unbinds the whole
+	 * LPASS chain) runtime-resumes the controller from
+	 * sdw_bus_master_add() before its bus is set up, and oopses in
+	 * sdw_bus_exit_clk_stop(). Runtime suspend already released hclk, so
+	 * release it here only if the controller is still active.
+	 */
+	pm_runtime_disable(dev);
+	if (!pm_runtime_status_suspended(dev))
+		clk_disable_unprepare(ctrl->hclk);
+	pm_runtime_set_suspended(dev);
 }
 
 static int __maybe_unused swrm_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
-- 
2.56.1

